{#
  The one definition of "what host is this?" for every Bay alert.

  Emitted as a bare display string with no shell or Python syntax, so the
  same file serves a bash assignment, a Python constant and a compose env
  entry. Symlinked into every role that names a host in an alert, because
  Ansible only searches the current role's templates/ — see _notify.sh.j2.

  Order: the operator's explicit label, the machine's own hostname, the
  inventory address. The last step is what makes this safe to adopt — an
  unlabelled host degrades to the name it already had, never to empty.

  The address rides along with the label because a responder needs both: the
  label to know WHICH box, the address to ssh into it. They collapse to one
  field when the label already IS the address, so a consumer that sets
  nothing sees no change in its alerts.

  Written with no trailing newline on purpose. It is interpolated inline.
#}
{%- set _bay_host_name = (bay_host_label | default("", true)) or (ansible_hostname | default("", true)) or (inventory_hostname | default("unknown")) -%}
{%- set _bay_host_addr = inventory_hostname | default("unknown") -%}
{{- _bay_host_name -}}{%- if _bay_host_name != _bay_host_addr %} ({{ _bay_host_addr }}){% endif -%}